.TH SDL_GetAsyncIOResult 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetAsyncIOResult \- Query an async I/O task queue for completed tasks.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_asyncio.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetAsyncIOResult(SDL_AsyncIOQueue *queue, SDL_AsyncIOOutcome *outcome);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If a task assigned to this queue has finished, this will return true and fill in
.BR outcome
with the details of the task\[char46] If no task in the queue has finished, this function will return false\[char46] This function does not block\[char46]
.PP
If a task has completed, this function will free its resources and the task pointer will no longer be valid\[char46] The task will be removed from the queue\[char46]
.PP
It is safe for multiple threads to call this function on the same queue at once; a completed task will only go to one of the threads\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I queue
the async I/O task queue to query\[char46]
.TP
.I outcome
details of a finished task will be written here\[char46] May not be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if a task has completed, false otherwise\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_WaitAsyncIOResult (3)
